description:
[narrowed from route-edit-f05460f2] In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/patch-with-tools.ts, make the semantic gate's PASSED line say WHY it passed.

WHY. verifyPatchAddressesGap fails open by design: it returns addresses:true when the judge is unreachable or its output unparseable, with the reason string recording which happened. The PASSED log line prints only the file, so a genuine judged pass and a judge-unavailable fail-open are indistinguishable in the journal.

That ambiguity has already materialised. Measured 2026-09-10: the gate's first PASSED at 10:37:50 on feature-compose.ts shows ZERO inference calls in the LLM vessel's journal in the surrounding 25 seconds — against 81 matching lines across the same session, so the grep is sound — and zero "skipped" lines, which rules out the explicit skip path. The most likely reading is a fail-open recorded as a pass. Until the reason is printed, the gate's protective value rests entirely on its refusals and its passes cannot be counted at all.

Make exactly ONE edit. Replace this single line, copied verbatim:

        console.log(`[pwt-semantic-gate] PASSED ${pointer.target_file}`);

with:

        // PRINT THE REASON, NOT JUST THE VERDICT. verifyPatchAddressesGap fails open —
        // addresses:true when the judge is unreachable or unparseable — and records which
        // in `reason`. Without it, "judged and passed" and "judge unavailable, failed open"
        // are the same log line, and the pass count measures nothing. Observed 2026-09-10:
        // the first PASSED had no inference call in the surrounding window.
        console.log(`[pwt-semantic-gate] PASSED ${pointer.target_file}: llm_consulted=${semVerdict.llm_consulted === true} reason=${String(semVerdict.reason ?? "(none)").slice(0, 200)}`);

Change nothing else. Do not touch the refusal branch above it, the resetTarget call, the vacuous-edit gate, the region-containment gate, or the staging code below.

SCOPE: semVerdict and pointer are both already in scope on the lines immediately around this one — semVerdict is the value returned by verifyPatchAddressesGap a few lines above, and its SemanticGateVerdict type carries both `reason` and `llm_consulted`.

